== 8.9 Chapter 8 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Maize is ready for harvest when],
  [the tassel first appears],
  [the leaves are still green],
  [the cob is half formed],
  [the husk dries and the grains harden]
)

#mcq(2, [The safe moisture content for storing maize grain is about],
  [12 to 13 per cent],
  [30 per cent],
  [5 per cent],
  [20 per cent]
)

#mcq(3, [Which of these is a maturity index?],
  [the type of soil],
  [the number of workers],
  [change in colour of the fruit],
  [the price at the market]
)

#mcq(4, [Harvesting a crop too late may result in],
  [a higher price with no cost],
  [shattering, rotting and pest damage in the field],
  [a larger root system],
  [a higher germination]
)

#mcq(5, [Gari is produced from cassava by],
  [boiling and mashing],
  [drying whole roots and milling],
  [soaking in brine only],
  [grating, fermenting, dewatering and frying]
)

#mcq(6, [Fermentation of cassava in gari production serves to],
  [add colour],
  [remove cyanogenic compounds and develop the sour taste],
  [increase the water content],
  [harden the starch]
)

#mcq(7, [Cocoa beans are fermented mainly to],
  [increase their weight],
  [dry them quickly],
  [develop flavour and colour and kill the germ],
  [remove the shell]
)

#mcq(8, [Rice is milled in order to],
  [add flavour],
  [increase the moisture],
  [remove the husk and bran],
  [kill the germ]
)

#mcq(9, [The first step in processing oil palm fruit is],
  [threshing the fruit from the bunch],
  [milling the fibre],
  [drying the kernel],
  [clarifying the oil]
)

#mcq(10, [Yam flour (elubo) is made by],
  [soaking in salt water],
  [fermenting and frying],
  [peeling, slicing, drying and milling],
  [boiling and mashing]
)

#mcq(11, [Processing a crop before sale is important because it],
  [adds value and extends shelf life],
  [reduces the price],
  [increases the moisture],
  [removes the need for storage]
)

#mcq(12, [A good store must be],
  [dry, cool, clean, sealed and raised],
  [warm and damp],
  [built of mud only],
  [open to the rain]
)

#mcq(13, [A maize crib is designed to],
  [hold threshed grain in bulk],
  [refrigerate the harvest],
  [allow air to circulate through the cobs],
  [keep the grain airtight]
)

#mcq(14, [Hermetic storage bags preserve grain by],
  [keeping the grain cold],
  [sealing out oxygen so that insects die],
  [poisoning the insects],
  [excluding light]
)

#mcq(15, [Silos are best suited to],
  [bulk grain storage on a large scale],
  [storing fresh vegetables],
  [holding yams in the ground],
  [drying cassava]
)

#mcq(16, [Yams are traditionally stored by],
  [drying them in the sun],
  [freezing them],
  [tying them in a barn or clamping them in the ground],
  [keeping them in water]
)

#mcq(17, [Which of these is the most important cause of storage loss in cowpea?],
  [birds],
  [the cowpea weevil],
  [nematodes],
  [rain in the field]
)

#mcq(18, [Grain that is stored too wet will],
  [become pest-free],
  [heat, mould and rot],
  [dry out and improve],
  [germinate in the bag]
)

#mcq(19, [Post-harvest loss is best defined as],
  [a fall in the market price],
  [any reduction in quantity or quality between field and consumer],
  [the cost of fertiliser],
  [the loss of the land to erosion]
)

#mcq(20, [Threshing on a tarpaulin rather than on the bare road reduces loss by],
  [killing insects],
  [drying the grain faster],
  [keeping the grain clean and preventing it being swept away],
  [increasing the moisture]
)

#mcq(21, [Which practice would reduce post-harvest loss most cheaply?],
  [building a silo],
  [hiring a lorry],
  [buying a cold room],
  [drying the grain properly before storage]
)

#mcq(22, [The channel of distribution for a food crop usually begins with the],
  [consumer],
  [wholesaler],
  [retailer],
  [farmer]
)

#mcq(23, [A middleman in the marketing chain performs the function of],
  [making the fertiliser],
  [producing the crop],
  [assembling, transporting and bearing risk],
  [fixing the rainfall]
)

#mcq(24, [Grading produce before sale is important because it],
  [kills pests],
  [reduces the moisture],
  [allows a higher price for a better quality lot],
  [increases the weight]
)

#mcq(25, [A marketing cooperative helps its members mainly by],
  [lending money at interest],
  [bulking produce and bargaining for a better price],
  [employing a manager for each member],
  [supplying land]
)

#mcq(26, [Which of these is a function of a cooperative rather than a credit union?],
  [keeping passbooks],
  [buying inputs in bulk and sharing the discount],
  [accepting members' savings],
  [lending at interest]
)

#mcq(27, [A farmer's share of the final price of a food crop is small mainly because],
  [he pays no tax],
  [the crop is bulkiest and the market thinnest where he sells],
  [the trader cheats him],
  [the government fixes the price]
)

#mcq(28, [Farm records are kept mainly in order to],
  [increase the yield directly],
  [satisfy the extension officer],
  [show whether the farm is making a profit],
  [attract rainfall]
)

#mcq(29, [An inventory record lists],
  [the names of the customers],
  [the rainfall for the year],
  [the prices at the market],
  [the land, tools, livestock and stock on hand]
)

#mcq(30, [A production record shows],
  [the market price],
  [the family's expenses],
  [the loan repayment schedule],
  [the area planted, inputs used and output obtained]
)

#mcq(31, [A farmer harvests 2 000 kg of maize; 15 per cent is lost in storage and the rest sells at ₦400 per kg. Revenue is],
  [₦340 000],
  [₦800 000],
  [₦1 700 000],
  [₦680 000]
)

#mcq(32, [Which of these losses occurs on the farm before storage even begins?],
  [weevil damage in the bag],
  [shattering at harvest],
  [rodent damage in the barn],
  [mould in the silo]
)

#mcq(33, [Curing is a post-harvest treatment applied to],
  [groundnut kernels],
  [cocoa beans],
  [maize grain],
  [onions, potatoes and yams]
)

#mcq(34, [Moisture meters are used at the drying floor to],
  [check that the grain is dry enough to store],
  [weigh the bags],
  [measure the yield],
  [count the insects]
)

#mcq(35, [Value addition to a farm product means],
  [storing it for a year],
  [processing it into a more valuable form before sale],
  [selling it as soon as it is harvested],
  [increasing the quantity sold]
)

#mcq(36, [Which of these would reduce a farmer's post-harvest loss in transport?],
  [delaying the journey in the rain],
  [using wet bags],
  [loading above the sides],
  [using sound bags and a covered load]
)

#mcq(37, [A warehouse differs from a crib mainly in that a warehouse],
  [stores bagged or processed produce in bulk],
  [holds maize on the cob],
  [is built of mud and thatch],
  [is used only for yams]
)

#mcq(38, [The price a farmer receives is best raised in the short term by],
  [selling immediately after harvest],
  [increasing the moisture content],
  [mixing good and poor produce],
  [grading, bulking and selling through a cooperative]
)

#mcq(39, [Which of these storage structures would best protect vegetables?],
  [a maize crib],
  [a yam barn],
  [a cold room],
  [an underground pit]
)

#mcq(40, [The main reason grain is winnowed after threshing is to],
  [polish the grain],
  [kill the weevils],
  [remove the chaff and lighter impurities],
  [increase the moisture]
)

